# Recover From Errors Helper

## File Purpose

This file provides standardized patterns and workflows for recovering from specific error types in front-end implementation. It should be consulted when:

- Implementation encounters specific, known error types
- Error patterns need specialized recovery strategies
- Debugging complex error situations
- Implementing error resilience patterns
- Recovering from runtime errors in production

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains error recovery guidance and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in message-commands:

```
recover-from-errors: @parameters/front-end/helpers/recovery/recover-from-errors.mdc
```

For more general recovery guidance, see:
- `recover-implementation.md`: General implementation recovery
- `fix-component-issues.md`: Component-specific issue fixes

## Error Recovery Process

### 1. Error Identification and Analysis

Begin by identifying and analyzing the specific error:

```typescript
// 1. Analyze error logs
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && cat logs/error.log | tail -n 50", false, false)

// 2. Check browser console errors
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run dev", false, true)

// 3. Analyze TypeScript errors
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run type-check", false, false)

// 4. Analyze test failures
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm test", false, false)

// 5. Check runtime errors in production
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run build && npm run start", false, true)
```

### 2. Categorize Error Type

Determine the specific category of the error for targeted recovery:

```typescript
// Analyze error patterns to categorize
grep_search("TypeError|ReferenceError|SyntaxError", false, "logs/error.log")
grep_search("Uncaught.*Error", false, "logs/error.log")
grep_search("Failed to compile", false, "logs/build.log")

// Check specific known error patterns
grep_search("Cannot read properties of (undefined|null)", false, "logs/error.log")
grep_search("Maximum update depth exceeded", false, "logs/error.log")
grep_search("Invalid hook call", false, "logs/error.log")
grep_search("Memory leak.*useEffect", false, "logs/error.log")
```

### 3. Apply Error-Specific Recovery Strategies

Apply recovery strategies based on the specific error type:

#### Type Errors (undefined/null)

