## Common Error Types and Recovery Strategies

### TypeScript/Type Errors

| Error | Recovery Strategy |
|-------|------------------|
| Cannot read properties of undefined | Add optional chaining (`?.`) and nullish coalescing (`??`) |
| Type 'X' is not assignable to type 'Y' | Add proper type guards and type assertions |
| No overload matches this call | Fix function parameter types to match defined signatures |
| Property does not exist on type | Add missing properties to interface or use proper type casting |
| Object is possibly undefined | Add null checks before accessing properties |

### React Errors

| Error | Recovery Strategy |
|-------|------------------|
| Invalid hook call | Move hooks to top level of component, fix conditional hook usage |
| Maximum update depth exceeded | Fix infinite loops in effects, add proper dependency arrays |
| Cannot update a component while rendering | Move state updates to effects or event handlers |
| Memory leak in component | Add cleanup functions to useEffect hooks |
| Each child should have a unique key | Add unique key prop to mapped elements |

### Build/Compile Errors

| Error | Recovery Strategy |
|-------|------------------|
| Module not found | Fix import paths, install missing dependencies |
| Cannot find module | Fix typos in import paths, create missing files |
| Unexpected token | Fix syntax errors, ensure correct syntax for the environment |
| Cannot use JSX | Add jsx configuration to tsconfig, install necessary dependencies |
| Unknown property on DOM element | Fix incorrect attribute names in JSX elements |

### Runtime Errors

| Error | Recovery Strategy |
|-------|------------------|
| API fetch errors | Add proper try/catch, implement retry logic |
| Cross-origin errors | Configure CORS headers, use proxy middleware |
| LocalStorage access errors | Add feature detection, handle private browsing mode |
| JSON parsing errors | Add try/catch for JSON.parse, validate response format |
| Code-splitting chunk loading errors | Add error boundaries, implement chunk loading retry |

## Error Prevention Patterns

### Defensive Programming

```typescript
// Type guard usage
import { isDefined, isArray } from '../utils/typeGuards';

// Before: direct property access
const count = data.items.length;

// After: defensive access with type guards
const count = isDefined(data) && isArray(data.items) ? data.items.length : 0;
```

### Error Boundaries

```typescript
// Component-level error boundaries
<ErrorBoundary fallback={<ErrorFallback />}>
  <ComponentThatMightError />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Feature-level error boundaries
<ErrorBoundary>
  <FeatureModule />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Route-level error boundaries
<ErrorBoundary>
  <Route path="/feature" component={FeatureComponent} />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

### Safe Data Access

```typescript
// Safe data access with utility functions
import { safeGet } from '../utils/typeGuards';

// Before: unsafe nested access
const userName = user.profile.details.name;

// After: safe access with default value
const userName = safeGet(user, 'profile.details.name', 'Unknown User');
```

### API Error Handling

```typescript
// Comprehensive API error handling
const fetchData = async () => {
  try {
    const response = await fetch('/api/data');
    
    // Handle HTTP errors
    if (!response.ok) {
      const errorBody = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));
      throw new Error(`API error: ${response.status} - ${errorBody.message || response.statusText}`);
    }
    
    // Handle unexpected response format
    const data = await response.json();
    if (!Array.isArray(data)) {
      throw new Error('Invalid response format: expected array');
    }
    
    return data;
  } catch (error) {
    // Handle network errors
    if (error.name === 'AbortError') {
      throw new Error('Request was aborted');
    }
    
    if (error.name === 'TypeError' && error.message.includes('NetworkError')) {
      throw new Error('Network error - please check your connection');
    }
    
    // Rethrow with additional context
    console.error('API error details:', error);
    throw error;
  }
};
```

